From: Astro <astro@muse.ai>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 20:15:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 18] qcacld-3.0: allow MAC change on monitor interfaces

wlan_mon_drv_ops lacks .ndo_set_mac_address, so `ip link set <mon>
address` fails with -EOPNOTSUPP ("Operation not supported") on monitor
interfaces. The normal wlan_drv_ops has it wired to hdd_set_mac_address.

Add the same handler to the monitor ops so MAC can be changed (while
the interface is down, as the handler requires) in monitor mode too.

diff --git a/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_main.c b/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_main.c
--- a/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_main.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_main.c
@@ -4962,6 +4962,7 @@ static const struct net_device_ops wlan_mon_drv_ops = {
 	.ndo_stop = hdd_stop,
 	.ndo_start_xmit = hdd_hard_start_xmit,
 	.ndo_get_stats = hdd_get_stats,
+	.ndo_set_mac_address = hdd_set_mac_address,
 };
 
 #ifdef WLAN_FEATURE_TSF_PTP
